Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Bluetooth: SMP: force legacy pairing when an LE legacy OOB TK is set

A stored LE legacy OOB Temporary Key (TK) only applies to legacy LE pairing.
To ensure pairing uses the correct method, clear the Secure Connections (SC)
bit in the authreq when building pairing commands for links that have a
stored legacy TK.

This is implemented automatically when le_legacy_tk_present is detected.
It is conservative (only affects paths where a legacy TK is present) and can
be converted to MGMT-driven/quirk-driven behavior later if requested.

Signed-off-by: Russell Oliver <roliver8143@gmail.com>
---
*** Begin Patch
*** Update File: net/bluetooth/smp.c
@@
 void build_pairing_cmd(struct smp *smp, u8 *cmd)
 {
     struct hci_conn *hcon = smp->hcon;
     u8 authreq = smp->authreq;
     u8 local_dist = smp->local_dist;
+    struct oob_data *oob = NULL;
 
+    /* If a stored LE legacy TK exists for this peer, prefer legacy pairing.
+     * Clear the Secure Connections (SC) bit so the TK is used in legacy flow.
+     */
+    if (hcon && hcon->type == LE_LINK) {
+        oob = hci_remote_oob_data_lookup(hcon->hdev, &hcon->dst);
+        if (oob && oob->le_legacy_tk_present)
+            authreq &= ~SMP_AUTH_SC;
+    }
+
     /* advertise OOB when smp was earlier marked as having OOB data */
     if (smp->oob_present)
         authreq |= SMP_OOB_PRESENT;
*** End Patch
